{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1504685483,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDEyMzYzMzE2NDI="},"added":["question"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1504686798,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyNzQxNDU2MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1796#issuecomment-327414560"},"message":"Sounds reasonable to me.\n\nHow would a query work? Are parsers supposed to actually perform the query on dumped metadata themselfes and report the query results? If so, a point \"query\" is missing in the list above.\nOtherwise: How exactly should parsers report on those dumps when asked for metadata to perform a query on? If they are the only ones to understand that dump, they need to report something different than just the dump. If the dump is, what is \"optimal for queries\" but then isn't actually used for queries, then this is confusing.\n\nOr maybe it's just me, who is confused right now. :-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1504695554,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyNzQ0OTI2OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1796#issuecomment-327449269"},"message":"Yes, \"query\" was intended to be covered by \"report metadata for a given list of dataset components (files/directories)\". But that would be some \"internal report\" to the `metadata` command, which would be the one and only user-facing API.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1504696382,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyNzQ1MjA2Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1796#issuecomment-327452063"},"message":"One of the growing issues with current approach seems to be scalability - already takes a while for an initial load and dump if a pickle. That is why I am not quite sure already either \"dump all relevant metadata in a format that is optimal for query\" ideas here are a relief or complication. \"each parser chose an optimal dump format that only itself needs to be able to understand\" somewhat suggest absent aggregation and unification which would delay things.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1504696610,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyNzQ1Mjg0Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1796#issuecomment-327452847"},"message":"FTR: There is no pickle anymore.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1504696660,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyNzQ1MzAwNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1796#issuecomment-327453006"},"message":"@yarikoptic I think the concern is universal, but what is the action plan from your POV?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1504697610,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyNzQ1NjAyMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1796#issuecomment-327456023"},"message":"\u003e Yes, \"query\" was intended to be covered by \"report metadata for a given list of dataset components (files/directories)\". But that would be some \"internal report\" to the metadata command\n\nIf I get it right, this means, that the actual query is done by `metadata` on the data reported by the parsers. Since only the parsers understand the dump, this report is not in that \"query optimized format\". So in what sense is it optimized for queries? May be it's just wording. Is \"optimized to answer the request on a given list of paths\" (which then is used for a query by `metadata`) a valid way to alternatively put it? Otherwise I don't fully get it yet, I guess.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1504698548,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyNzQ1OTE2NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1796#issuecomment-327459164"},"message":"Maybe better discussed in a hangout...","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1504698554,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDEyMzY2NjQ3NDk="},"added":["conference agenda item"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1504711721,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyNzUyMTAwMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1796#issuecomment-327521003"},"message":"Mental notes:\n\n- Parsers need to be able to report their own metadata key definitions that are stored alongside the dataset-global metadata (from a metadata homogenization POV it is worthwhile goal to avoid ANY sort of addtional metadata _key_ definitions)\n- Parsers store file-based metadata as key-value mappings, where\n   - keys are regex that match relative paths within a dataset (this enables efficient storage of hierarchical metadata schemes like BIDS)\n   - values are key-value mappings with metadata, where\n      - keys are defined, homogenized keys (see point 1)\n      - values are arbitrary metadata values\n\n- metadata aggregation of file-based metadata involves gathering all metadata from all parsers. Metadata merges are performed (in the same way it is already done for dataset-global metadata) for each unique regex (it is theoretically possible to generate regexes for all unique subsets, but that can be a CS student's contribution, as would be compacting metadata from less efficient native metadata schemes, e.g. one set per file with lots of redundancy)\n- metadata access involves going through all regexes, find the ones that match the path in question and report the union of all associated metadata\n\nThis strategy enforces metadata key homogenization (we only store one set of metadata, not one per type) -- homogenized metadata should be more useful anyways.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1507443421,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzNDk4NjAxOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1796#issuecomment-334986018"},"message":"No final verdict from @yarikoptic still, but given that we are months into the process -\u003e close.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1507443421,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTI4MzA4Nzk0OA=="},"status":2}]}